  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction (NAICS 237310) shows active federal contracting in FY2026 to date. The NAICS class has $2.2B in obligations across 2,094 awards, with an average award size of $1.1M. Obligations are up 90.6% year over year. Department of Transportation is the largest buyer with $787M in obligations, followed by Department of Defense with $646M and Department of Agriculture with $536M. KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO leads vendors with $297M in obligations. The FY21 through FY26 series shows FY23 at $2.8B as the high point, and FY25 at $1.2B as the low point prior to the current year. The NAICS class includes a broad set of buying agencies, with the Department of the Interior at $192M and smaller buyers such as the Environmental Protection Agency at $1.1M. Vendors beyond the top performer include AMRIZE SOUTHWEST INC with $96.4M and BFBC LLC with $86.4M. This snapshot reflects fiscal-year-to-date totals and contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
